---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import Link from '../components/Link.astro';
import MethodMarkers from '../components/MethodMarkers.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../components/FinalCTA.astro';
import { transformation } from '../data/method';
---

<Base
  title="The Matchbook Method"
  description="Twelve connected growth areas. A clearer picture of your business. Explore the Matchbook Method and the path from scattered activity to a prioritized growth plan."
>
  <section class="method-hero dark-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="method-hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">The Matchbook Method</p>
        <h1>
          12 moves.
          <br />
          One growth
          <br />
          <em>engine.</em>
        </h1>
        <p>
          See the whole business.
          <br />
          Find what matters.
          <br />
          Know where to go next.
        </p>
        <Link
          href="/contact?interest=The%20Matchbook%20Method"
          variant="button"
          light
        >
          Put the Method to work
        </Link>
      </div>
      <Photo
        kind="match"
        class="single-match"
        eager
        sizes="(max-width: 700px) 40vw, 45vw"
      />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="method-intro wrap section-space">
    <p class="eyebrow">The pieces are connected.</p>
    <h2>
      A marketing problem
      <br />
      can start <em>somewhere else.</em>
    </h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        Low inquiries could point to an unclear offer. A strong campaign can
        lose people on a confusing website. More new customers won’t resolve an
        experience that gives them little reason to return.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Matchbook Method examines the interconnected areas that influence
        growth. It brings them into one conversation so you can see where to
        focus.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="method-system section-space">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What we look at</p>
        <h2>
          Twelve areas.
          <br />
          <em>The whole picture.</em>
        </h2>
        <p>
          Each matters on its own.
          <br />
          The opportunity is in how they work together.
        </p>
      </div>
      <MethodMarkers expanded />
      <p class="system-note">
        A view of the areas we explore—not a checklist to complete in order.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="uncover wrap section-space">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">What a closer look can reveal</p>
      <h2>
        Sometimes the next move
        <br />
        <em>is hiding in plain sight.</em>
      </h2>
      <p>
        Every business is different. These are examples of opportunities the
        Method is designed to explore, not findings or promised results.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="uncover-list">
      <article>
        <span class="micro">The offer</span>
        <h3>A great service that’s hard to understand.</h3>
        <p>
          A clearer way to describe and package it may help the right customer
          see its value.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="micro">The handoff</span>
        <h3>Interest that never becomes a conversation.</h3>
        <p>
          The opportunity may be in the step between discovery, inquiry, and
          follow-up.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="micro">The relationship</span>
        <h3>A customer who could have a reason to return.</h3>
        <p>
          Customer experience, retention, and partnerships may deserve attention
          alongside acquisition.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="blueprint-section dark-section section-space">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="blueprint-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What you walk away with</p>
        <h2>
          Your Matchbook
          <br />
          <em>Growth Blueprint.</em>
        </h2>
        <p>
          A clear view of the business today, a prioritized set of
          recommendations, and a practical growth roadmap. Something you can use
          to make the next decision.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="transformation">
        {transformation.map((step, i) => (
          <li>
            <span class="micro">0{i + 1}</span>
            <span>{step}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <div class="blueprint-output">
        <p>
          <strong>Clarity.</strong>
          <br />
          Understand the opportunities and gaps.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Priorities.</strong>
          <br />
          Know where your attention belongs.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>A roadmap.</strong>
          <br />
          Connect the next steps to the bigger picture.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="method-next wrap section-space">
    <p class="eyebrow">What happens next</p>
    <h2>
      A plan is a beginning.
      <br />
      <em>Let’s put it to work.</em>
    </h2>
    <p>
      Take the roadmap forward with your team, or talk with us about the
      creative, social, and ongoing growth support that would help you implement
      it.
    </p>
    <Link href="/services">Explore support beyond the strategy</Link>
  </section>
  <FinalCTA />
</Base>
